# v3: E3 go/no-go on the frozen grid (answering idea-review-repo#5)

**Correction to v2.** v2 took `sbatch --test-only` start estimates (GPU 2026-10-24) as the queue forecast; they are wrong for short jobs. `sacct` for the six E3 pilot/init jobs (53920500, 53920920/1, 53921153/4, 53921685, all 1xV100/GPU, time limits 40 min-2 h) shows submit-to-start waits of 3, 4, 4, 2, 2, 4 min. `--test-only` still says 2026-10-24 now for a 4 h job, so it is unreliable here and only the measured waits count. Basis: 6 samples on one evening, time limits <= 2 h. A long time limit or heavy use of the shared account (pi-gaox, fair-share) can change this.

**Q1 Ibex dependency: GO**, with conditions:
- Submit independent, resumable per-config jobs (3 seeds packed), each with time limit <= 2 h (the limit under which all measured jobs started within minutes), as an array; do not submit one long job.
- Fallback trigger: if no must-have Arm P job has started 60 min after submission, or fewer than half of the submitted must-have jobs have finished 12 h after the first start, start the CPU fallback in parallel (do not wait to cancel Ibex).
- Fallback adequacy: marginal. 0.75 s/step is the best case; the measured 10 s/step under host load makes 54 runs x 1560 steps ~ 240 h, which is infeasible. Keep the fallback only for what a few CPU jobs finish: order predictor, target update, masking, then wd; 3 seeds on the factor extremes first, and say in the paper which cells ran on which resource and at what horizon. Do not shorten to 8 of 100/50 epochs inside the warmup: scale the schedule to the horizon.
**Q2 20 of 50 epochs: FITS.** 3900 steps x 0.16 s = ~10.4 min per config (3 seeds packed) matches the quoted 11 min; 34 configs ~ 6.2 GPU-h, ~7 with overheads, ~10 with interventions and full-length runs, and a re-run of the whole grid costs about the same again, which is affordable once, not repeatedly. Define in the plan exactly what "20 of 50" is (stop at epoch 20 of the 50-epoch schedule, so the lr/wd/EMA values at the stop are those of epoch 20 of the 50-epoch run) and use that horizon for the pre-registered thresholds; the probe and full-length claims are about the 50-epoch runs only.
**Conditions before any sweep launches:** (1) `results/e3/prediction.json` committed first, including a sign or an explicit "no predicted difference" null for every mask setting; (2) code and metric definitions frozen at a recorded commit, each run result carrying config, seed, code commit and package versions; (3) the Ibex environment's torch and other packages pinned to releases <= 2026-09-01 (torch <= 2.13.0), checked on Ibex; (4) the Arm P / Arm T results labelled as separate arms in every table (AdamW+LN recipe vs plain SGD), since the theory is gradient-flow and only Arm T is the direct test.
**Cut order unchanged:** Arm T factor sweeps beyond wd, then the C4 interventions; Arm P must-have factors are never cut. Judge the result by what is measured; a failed prediction is reported as such.
